{
  "slug": "one-armed-bandit",
  "title": "One-armed bandit: one committed pull",
  "kind": "coin_puzzle",
  "security_scope": "Original WIP teaching game for issue #20, testnet teaching only and not ready for real funds. One pull coin holds exactly 8,000 mojos (the player's 1,000-mojo bet plus the house reserve) and curries one proper list: house payout hash, sha256(seed domain || house seed), player payout hash and the player's 32-byte salt. The house publishes its seed commitment before the player picks a salt. Before the coin is ten blocks old the house may resolve by revealing the seed: the outcome byte sha256(spin domain || seed || salt)[31] pays 7 bets below 16, 2 bets below 64 and nothing otherwise (expected return 208/256 = 81.25%), and the house receives the rest. At or after ten blocks the player may claim the whole pull, so a house that withholds its reveal forfeits its reserve. Consensus enforces ages and amounts; the puzzle only emits conditions.",
  "environment": "strict",
  "reference_mode": "module",
  "provenance": {
    "classification": "original teaching implementation",
    "references": [
      "https://chialisp.com/conditions/",
      "https://chialisp.com/chialisp-currying/",
      "https://github.com/judeallred/chialisp-oxide/issues/20"
    ],
    "source_origin": "All four paired source files (Rust export, independent Chialisp reference, Rue port and Python oracle) are original implementations of this explicit teaching contract. No published slot-machine puzzle is copied or ported; the slug avoids the unrelated slot-machine action-layer name.",
    "limitations": [
      "The house must use a fresh unpredictable seed for every pull. A reused or guessable seed lets the player choose a winning salt; the puzzle cannot detect reuse.",
      "The player must pick the salt only after the commitment is published; the commitment and salt are both curried when the pull coin is created.",
      "One fixed bet and paytable; there is no bankroll singleton, multi-line reels or house close-out here. The host funds each pull with exactly the bet plus reserve.",
      "SHA-256 is an assumption; proof models do not cover SHA or this game. The stated return is exact arithmetic over the paytable, not a fairness proof."
    ]
  },
